  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A drink is called fanta-like if the last three letters of its name are ′n′,′t′,\\tt{'n'}, \\tt{'t'},′n′,′t′, and ′a′\\tt{'a'}′a′, in that order.\n\nThat is, the name of the drink must end with `nta`.\n\nYou bought a drink from a vending machine.\n\nThe name of the drink is represented by the string SSS.\n\nIt is guaranteed that SSS consists of **exactly 555** lowercase English letters.\n\nIs the drink fanta-like?\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input contains a single string SSS of length 555, denoting the name of the drink you bought.\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint the answer: YES\\tt{YES}YES if the drink is fanta-like, and NO\\tt{NO}NO otherwise.\n\n\nEach character of the output may be printed in either uppercase or lowercase, i.e. the strings NO,nO,No,\\tt{NO}, \\tt{nO}, \\tt{No},NO,nO,No, and no\\tt{no}no will all be treated as equivalent.",
    "constraints": [
      "SSS consists of exactly 555 lowercase English letters."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "fonta",
        "output": "Yes",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe last three letters of \"fonta\"\\tt{\"fonta\"}\"fonta\" are nta, so it is fanta-like."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "pasta",
        "output": "No",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe last three letters of \"pasta\"\\tt{\"pasta\"}\"pasta\" are sta, so it is not fanta-like."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "plant",
        "output": "No",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe last three letters of \"plant\"\\tt{\"plant\"}\"plant\" are ant, so it is not fanta-like.\nNote that even though it has the three letters n, t, and a, they are not in the correct order."
      }
    ]
  },
